course: dictionary
lesson: 14118
title: Tiny words: micro
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Micro means very small. You will see it at the start of many words, and it often tells you that something is tiny. «The garden had a micro farm with six little plants.» The word micro tells you the farm is very small, so you can picture its size.
explain: Micro- at the start of a word is a prefix, a small word part that changes the meaning of the word after it. A microscope is a tool that makes tiny things look bigger. A microphone makes small sounds louder. A microchip is a very small piece of computer, and micro-organisms are tiny living things you can only see with a microscope.
explain: In science, micro- can also mean one millionth. A micrometre is one millionth of a metre, so it is incredibly small. Notice how the meaning stays close to small, even when the number is exact.
fact: Micro means very small.
fact: Micro- is a prefix, a word part added to the front of a word.
fact: A microscope is a tool that makes tiny things look bigger.
fact: In science, micro- means one millionth, as in micrometre.
fact: Informally, «a micro» can be a short name for a small computer, a microwave oven, or the micro:bit used in schools.
exercise: «The scientist used a microscope to look at a drop of pond water.» What is a microscope for? | *Making tiny things look bigger | Playing music loudly | Cooking food quickly | Weighing a bag of shopping
exercise: «Mia's micro scooter folds up small enough to fit in her bag.» What does micro mean here? | Very fast | Very old | Very heavy | *Very small
exercise: «We heated the soup in the microwave.» Find and copy the word that starts with micro. | the | *microwave | soup | heated
test: «Sam programmed the micro:bit to light up when he pressed the button.» What is a micro:bit? | A large kitchen oven | A big bird | A type of bicycle | *A small computer used in schools
test: In science, a micrometre is a very tiny length. What fraction of a metre is it? | *One millionth of a metre | One hundredth of a metre | One metre | One thousand of a metre
exam: In «microchip», what does micro- tell you? | Very big | Very wet | Very old | *Very small
